WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:06.340
"Groatzempic: Using Intact
Grains to Boost GLP-1"

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:07.641
In my last few videos,

00:00:07.641 --> 00:00:09.810
I talked about using prebiotics,
like fiber,

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.678
to deliver nutrients
to the colon

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.914
for the sustained
and prolonged release

00:00:13.914 --> 00:00:17.551
of appetite-reducing
gut hormones like GLP-1.

00:00:17.551 --> 00:00:20.254
That’s because the majority
of cells producing GLP-1

00:00:20.254 --> 00:00:22.055
are located
at the end of the gut,

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:23.824
in our large intestine.

00:00:23.824 --> 00:00:26.093
But prebiotics
don’t represent the only

00:00:26.093 --> 00:00:28.962
"slow digestion-oriented
dietary strategy"

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:31.665
to sustain
the secretion of GLP-1.

00:00:31.665 --> 00:00:34.334
Prebiotics can be used
to promote metabolic health

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:37.871
and longevity by stimulating
intestinal production of GLP-1,

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:41.475
and so too
can the drug Acarbose,

00:00:41.475 --> 00:00:43.210
which acts as a starch blocker,

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:45.812
inhibiting the enzymes
that would normally digest

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:48.615
carbohydrates earlier
in the small intestine.

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:51.885
Acarbose-induced transfer
of carbs to the lower parts

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:55.055
of the intestine
increases GLP-1 levels.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:58.091
And since changes in GLP-1
correlate with weight loss

00:00:58.091 --> 00:00:59.293
in those on the drug,

00:00:59.293 --> 00:01:02.296
it’s reasonable to suspect
that GLP-1 is a mediator

00:01:02.296 --> 00:01:04.898
of the favorable impact
of acarbose therapy

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.934
on weight control.

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:11.238
There’s also a third strategy,
eating "lente" carbohydrates,

00:01:11.238 --> 00:01:13.907
from the Latin lentus for slow.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:18.111
Instead of taking a drug to slow
dietary carbohydrate digestion,

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:19.746
what about just choosing a diet

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:22.950
centered around slow-digesting
"lente" carbohydrates

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.952
to achieve comparable benefits?

00:01:24.952 --> 00:01:26.586
That’s the theory, anyway.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:29.222
So, that means pasta,
beans, groats,

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:31.992
meaning structurally intact
grain kernels,

00:01:31.992 --> 00:01:33.760
as well as sprouted grains.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.462
Let’s start with beans.

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:38.598
Here, researchers found
enhanced secretion

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:40.400
of satiety-promoting
gut hormones

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.636
after the consumption
of white bread

00:01:42.636 --> 00:01:46.440
that had been enriched with
coarsely ground chickpea flour,

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.442
and the more chickpea
it contained,

00:01:48.442 --> 00:01:50.911
the higher
the GLP-1 levels spiked,

00:01:50.911 --> 00:01:53.213
but where are you going
to find chickpea bread?

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:55.649
What about just eating beans?

00:01:55.649 --> 00:01:57.818
Asking people to eat five cups
(850-900 g) of beans a week

00:01:57.818 --> 00:01:59.987
spontaneously led
to health benefits

00:01:59.987 --> 00:02:01.655
similar to those seen
after asking people

00:02:01.655 --> 00:02:04.725
to cut 500 calories
out of their daily diet,

00:02:04.725 --> 00:02:07.894
but there was no change
in GLP-1 levels.

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:10.197
What about cocoa beans?

00:02:10.197 --> 00:02:12.866
I wish, but sadly,
no effect of dark chocolate

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:14.935
on GLP-1 either.

00:02:14.935 --> 00:02:18.839
The one pasta study I could find
also failed to bump GLP-1,

00:02:18.839 --> 00:02:21.241
but the one
sprouted grain study I found

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:24.544
showed higher GLP-1 response
to sprouted bread,

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:26.146
compared to four other types
of bread,

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:29.716
which didn’t differ
significantly from each other.

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:31.351
Eleven- or 12-grain bread

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:33.787
was no different
than white bread?

00:02:33.787 --> 00:02:36.156
That’s what’s generally found
when comparing products

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:39.393
made with whole-grain flour
to refined-grain flour;

00:02:39.393 --> 00:02:42.129
there aren’t any immediate
right-after-the-meal effects

00:02:42.129 --> 00:02:44.898
of whole wheat bread compared
to white bread, for example.

00:02:44.898 --> 00:02:46.166
You can’t just eat bread

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:49.369
and expect some kind
of "doughzempic" effect,

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:51.705
because, as I explained
in my last few videos,

00:02:51.705 --> 00:02:55.976
food structure is critical
for optimal health.

00:02:55.976 --> 00:02:58.045
When grains are milled
into flour,

00:02:58.045 --> 00:02:59.946
whether whole wheat or white,

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:03.050
their cell walls are ruptured
and the starch spills out

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:04.718
and never makes it
down to our colon;

00:03:04.718 --> 00:03:06.987
so, we don’t get
their added benefit.

00:03:06.987 --> 00:03:07.921
This is one of the reasons

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:10.757
former Harvard nutrition chair
Walt Willett

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:13.326
has argued that the term
whole grain

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:18.398
should probably be reserved for
only whole intact grain kernels,

00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:22.536
otherwise known as groats,
the "wholiest" of grains.

00:03:22.536 --> 00:03:26.073
In my book How Not to Diet,
I talk about my BROL bowl,

00:03:26.073 --> 00:03:28.675
a prebiotic mix
that includes barley groats,

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:30.310
rye groats, and oat groats.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:33.814
What effect might they have
on GLP-1?

00:03:33.814 --> 00:03:35.282
If you give people bread

00:03:35.282 --> 00:03:38.652
containing some
whole intact barley groats,

00:03:38.652 --> 00:03:41.088
there’s no immediate difference
in GLP-1 levels

00:03:41.088 --> 00:03:42.622
in the subsequent three hours,

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:44.758
but the groats
wouldn’t even have had time

00:03:44.758 --> 00:03:46.993
to make it down to your colon
that quickly.

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:48.895
However,
after your good bacteria

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:51.431
have had a chance
to break open their cell walls,

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:54.101
you get a greater,
higher GLP-1 bump

00:03:54.101 --> 00:03:59.005
more than 12 hours later,
at breakfast the next day.

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:00.040
The question, though,

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:03.176
is whether that translates
into a suppressed appetite.

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:07.047
And indeed, lower food intake
not just at breakfast,

00:04:07.047 --> 00:04:11.218
but also at lunch the next day,
14 hours later!

00:04:11.218 --> 00:04:14.154
Having barley kernels
at an evening meal

00:04:14.154 --> 00:04:16.556
not only increased GLP-1
the next day,

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:19.426
boosting blood levels
by 43 percent at breakfast,

00:04:19.426 --> 00:04:21.128
but feelings of hunger
decreased

00:04:21.128 --> 00:04:22.662
during the entire next day,

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:25.165
and the research participants
ate about 100 fewer calories

00:04:25.165 --> 00:04:27.234
of an all-you-can-eat lunch,

00:04:27.234 --> 00:04:29.136
just because they had
some barley groats

00:04:29.136 --> 00:04:31.905
fourteen hours before.

00:04:31.905 --> 00:04:33.874
Eat barley groats
three days in row

00:04:33.874 --> 00:04:37.110
and on the fourth day
see a 56 percent increase

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:40.080
in the level of GLP-1
in your blood.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.082
What about rye groats?

00:04:42.082 --> 00:04:44.985
Eat rye groats for supper,
and more than 10 hours later,

00:04:44.985 --> 00:04:49.022
your GLP-1 levels are up,
and your appetite is down.

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:50.290
Researchers found
that participants

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:52.626
had an increased
subjective feeling of satiety

00:04:52.626 --> 00:04:55.095
during the course
of the entire next day.

00:04:55.095 --> 00:04:57.631
So, rye groats
"demonstrate anti-diabetes

00:04:57.631 --> 00:04:59.132
and anti-obesity potential

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.434
as manifested by
enhanced blood sugar control

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.903
and increased GLP-1

00:05:02.903 --> 00:05:05.872
and the accompanying
appetite suppression."

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:06.840
And there was a correlation

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:08.141
between the short-chain
fatty acids,

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:11.011
acetate and propionate,
and GLP-1 response,

00:05:11.011 --> 00:05:12.078
suggesting that, indeed,

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:14.781
we may have
our good gut bugs to thank

00:05:14.781 --> 00:05:17.083
for the beneficial effects.

